.TITLE "defaults"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Manages the macOS user defaults system, which stores application and system preferences
in property list (plist) files. This command allows reading, writing, and deleting
default settings for applications and system services from the command line.
It is a powerful tool for configuring macOS behavior.

.DIV "ALIAS"
**pref**

.DIV "TLDR"
**defaults read __com.apple.finder__**
Reads all preferences for a specific application domain, e.g., __com.apple.finder__.
> __com.apple.finder__: The domain identifier for the application or service.

**defaults read __com.apple.finder__ __key__**
Reads the value of a specific __key__ within an application domain.
> __com.apple.finder__: The domain identifier. | __key__: The preference key to read.

**defaults write __com.apple.finder__ __key__ __"value"__**
Writes a __"value"__ to a specific __key__ within an application domain.
> __com.apple.finder__: The domain identifier. | __key__: The preference key to write. | __"value"__: The value to set for the key.

**defaults delete __com.apple.finder__ __key__**
Deletes a specific __key__ from an application domain.
> __com.apple.finder__: The domain identifier. | __key__: The preference key to delete.

.DIV "SUMMARY"
The `defaults` command provides granular control over macOS preferences.
Changes made with `defaults write` often require the affected application
to be restarted or the user to log out and back in for them to take effect.
It is an essential tool for system administrators and power users.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:open**

